<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kido Takayoshi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833–1877</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Katsura Kogorō</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kido Takayoshi (1833–1877), also known as Katsura Kogorō, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> of the Chōshū domain and one of the three great leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a>. He negotiated the Satchō Alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> in 1866 and helped draft the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charter-oath">Charter Oath</a> of 1868. In the new government he pressed for the return of the domains to the emperor and their abolition in 1871, and he took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwakura-mission">Iwakura Mission</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kido-takayoshi.jpg" alt="Kido Takayoshi" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Takayoshi_Kido_suit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
